    <p class="chapter-head__kicker">Chapter {String(ch.num).padStart(2, '0')}</p>
    <h1>{ch.title}</h1>
    <p class="chapter-head__lead">The scientific program of the conference is designed as a journey through the core questions of modern physics. Moving beyond the boundaries of isolated subfields, the program encourages an intellectual journey where the laws of the subatomic world, the patterns of complexity, and the architecture of the cosmos continuously echo and challenge one another.</p>
  </header>

  <article class="prose">
    <p>The conference is structured across <strong>two parallel historical and academic hubs</strong>, each embodying a distinct approach to the physical reality: Torino and Milano.</p>
    <p>Torino will serve as the core venue for Nuclear, Complex System Physics, and Advanced Technological Physics, whereas Milano will concentrate on the frontiers of Particle, Astrophysics, and Biomedical Physics.</p>
    <p>By design, this dual-hub structure mirrors the very nature of scientific progress: a constant dialogue between the abstract and the concrete. While the mind conceives universes in the silence of theoretical calculation, the hand builds the tools to observe them with artisanal alacrity. The program will showcase scientific excellence across theoretical, experimental, computational, and applied physics.</p>
    <p>A defining feature of the scientific program will be <strong>the synergy between renowned Italian keynote speakers and distinguished international experts</strong>. Some of Italy's most influential physicists, alongside leading global scientists, currently head major international collaborations around the world. Their diverse participation will provide attendees with a unique perspective on the global scientific landscape, making the conference <strong>a crossroads of ideas and perspectives</strong>.</p>
    <p>Through this choice, we aim to inspire participants by presenting outstanding examples of scientific achievement both locally and globally, showcasing our academic foundations while building international bridges and connecting students.</p>

